Why Is Demand Increasing?

Analog-to-digital converters remain essential for converting real-world signals into digital data used by modern electronic systems.

Demand is supported by medical imaging, automotive electronics, communications, industrial automation and consumer electronics.

Higher-resolution conversion, faster sampling and lower power consumption are becoming increasingly important as electronic systems process larger volumes of sensor and measurement data.

Fab & Technology Pulse

Technology development is focused on higher resolution at lower power, faster sampling and tighter analog-front-end integration. These improvements allow ADCs to support increasingly demanding sensing, communications and control applications.

